    what: "M7 (#925): an iron pickaxe at level 2 with the fourth modifier spent into a slot leveling granted -- forgeweave:tool_level is {level, xp, bonus_slots} (absent means level 0, so pre-M7 tools need no migration) and bonus_slots is stored rather than recomputed from level, so retuning defaultBaseXP or levelMultiplier never strips a slot a tool already earned (D-M7-1). Three default slots hold searing/magnetic_pull/resonant and aquadynamic sits in the first earned one, which is what makes this fixture prove the slot/modifier interaction decodes and not just the component. forgeweave:tool_id is the ledger UUID DamageXpLedger mints the first time a tool banks damage on a target it did not kill (D-M7-4); the ledger itself lives in entity NBT and is pinned by ToolXpGameTests#theDamageLedgerSurvivesAnEntitySaveAndReload instead -- see SaveCompatCorpusTest's javadoc. Printed off the real stack in a GameTest and then stripped of the vanilla minecraft:tool component, whose block-tag references need the full tag data a real server loads and this corpus's lightweight registry bootstrap does not, the same omission m777_tool_pickaxe_base_tier.snbt and m2_tool_pickaxe_modifiers.snbt make."
